{"name":"Caspian Sea","hex":"#4f6f91","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Caspian Sea","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A landlocked sea (properly a saline lake) between Eastern Europe and Asia, and the Earth’s largest inland body of water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Caspian_Sea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Caspian Sea","blocks":[{"text":"The Caspian Sea is the world's largest inland body of water, also described as the world's largest lake and usually referred to as a full-fledged sea. An endorheic basin, it is situated in both Europe and Asia: east of the Caucasus, west of the broad steppe of Central Asia, south of the fertile plains of Southern Russia in Eastern Europe, and north of the mountainous Iranian Plateau. It covers a surface area of 371,000 km2 (143,244 sq mi), an area similar to Japan, with a volume of 78,200 km3 (19,000 cu mi). It has a salinity of approximately 1.2%, about a third of the salinity of average seawater. It is bounded by Kazakhstan to the northeast, Russia to the northwest, Azerbaijan to the southwest, Iran to the south, and Turkmenistan to the southeast. The name of the Caspian Sea is derived from the ancient Iranic Caspi people."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Caspian_Sea_from_orbit.jpg/330px-Caspian_Sea_from_orbit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caspian_Sea"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Paratethys_Megalake_Infographic_23X_2_EN.jpg/500px-Paratethys_Megalake_Infographic_23X_2_EN.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Paratethys_Megalake_Infographic_23X_2_EN.jpg/1280px-Paratethys_Megalake_Infographic_23X_2_EN.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Paratethys_Megalake_Infographic_23X_2_EN.jpg/500px-Paratethys_Megalake_Infographic_23X_2_EN.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Separation of the Paratethys Sea from open seas formed a megalake, the basis of the Caspian Sea and other bodies of water in vicinity, resulting in confinements of oceanic faunas such as cetaceans and pinnipeds.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AParatethys_Megalake_Infographic_23X_2_EN.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/CaspianSeaDrainage_v1.png/500px-CaspianSeaDrainage_v1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/CaspianSeaDrainage_v1.png/500px-CaspianSeaDrainage_v1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Area around the Caspian Sea. Yellow area indicates the (approximate) drainage area.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACaspianSeaDrainage_v1.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Caspian_Sea_Kazakhstan_Mangistau.jpg/500px-Caspian_Sea_Kazakhstan_Mangistau.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Caspian_Sea_Kazakhstan_Mangistau.jpg/500px-Caspian_Sea_Kazakhstan_Mangistau.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Caspian Sea near Aktau, Mangystau Region, Kazakhstan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACaspian_Sea_Kazakhstan_Mangistau.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Area_reductions_arising_from_sea_level_decline_scenarios_for_ecologically_important_areas_in_the_Caspian_Sea.png/500px-Area_reductions_arising_from_sea_level_decline_scenarios_for_ecologically_important_areas_in_the_Caspian_Sea.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Area_reductions_arising_from_sea_level_decline_scenarios_for_ecologically_important_areas_in_the_Caspian_Sea.png/500px-Area_reductions_arising_from_sea_level_decline_scenarios_for_ecologically_important_areas_in_the_Caspian_Sea.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Area reductions arising from sea level decline scenarios for ecologically important areas in the Caspian Sea","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArea_reductions_arising_from_sea_level_decline_scenarios_for_ecologically_important_areas_in_the_Caspian_Sea.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Ghaleye_Rud_Khan_%2840%29_4.jpg/500px-Ghaleye_Rud_Khan_%2840%29_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Ghaleye_Rud_Khan_%2840%29_4.jpg/1280px-Ghaleye_Rud_Khan_%2840%29_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Ghaleye_Rud_Khan_%2840%29_4.jpg/500px-Ghaleye_Rud_Khan_%2840%29_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Iran's northern Caspian Hyrcanian mixed forests are maintained by moisture captured from the Caspian Sea by